<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tumkur</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tumakuru</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tumkur, officially Tumakuru, is a city in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, about 70 km north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengaluru">Bengaluru</a> and the headquarters of Tumkur district. The surrounding area formed part of Nolambavadi, ruled by the Nolamba dynasty in the 9th and 10th centuries, and later came under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysalas</a>, Vijayanagara and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a>. It is home to the Siddaganga Math, a major <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lingayatism">Lingayat</a> monastery.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tumkur.jpg" alt="Tumkur" width="320" height="582" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AkshayAnand · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tumkur_Montage.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
